1
00:00:00,128 --> 00:00:05,810
FILING FOR LOVE

2
00:00:25,284 --> 00:00:26,285
Bye, then.

3
00:00:26,577 --> 00:00:27,995
Would you like some coffee?

4
00:00:28,413 --> 00:00:29,580
No. It's late.

5
00:00:29,914 --> 00:00:32,083
Have a cup of cold water, then.

6
00:00:32,166 --> 00:00:33,459
You must be exhausted.

7
00:00:40,341 --> 00:00:41,676
He's pretty hefty.

8
00:00:42,927 --> 00:00:44,303
You're quite strong.

9
00:00:45,805 --> 00:00:47,265
I do what must be done.

10
00:00:47,598 --> 00:00:48,641
Thanks for the water.

11
00:00:53,896 --> 00:00:56,149
Ki-jun and I live together.

12
00:00:58,526 --> 00:00:59,902
It would seem so.

13
00:00:59,986 --> 00:01:01,070
Don't get the wrong idea.

14
00:01:01,154 --> 00:01:04,157
I asked to stay just for a while
due to some personal reasons.

15
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:05,491
Ki-jun and I are just...

16
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,201
We're just friends.

17
00:01:07,493 --> 00:01:08,494
For now, that is.

18
00:01:09,787 --> 00:01:11,456
We used to date for a bit.

19
00:01:13,583 --> 00:01:14,584
I see.

20
00:01:17,336 --> 00:01:19,672
Thanks. Sorry for the late intrusion.

21
00:01:45,198 --> 00:01:46,365
What are you doing, Joo In-a?

22
00:01:47,909 --> 00:01:48,951
Get a hold of yourself.

23
00:01:55,249 --> 00:01:58,711
EPISODE 6:
CAN'T YOU

24
00:02:00,379 --> 00:02:01,672
{\an8}Noh Ki-jun, wake up.

25
00:02:01,964 --> 00:02:04,091
{\an8}You can share my taxi
if you get ready in ten minutes.

26
00:02:04,217 --> 00:02:06,135
{\an8}My headache's killing me.

27
00:02:07,303 --> 00:02:08,638
{\an8}How did I get home last night?

28
00:02:09,805 --> 00:02:10,848
{\an8}You just did.

29
00:02:12,892 --> 00:02:14,310
Let's just go straight to work.

30
00:02:15,811 --> 00:02:17,438
{\an8}My homing instinct never fails.

31
00:02:18,689 --> 00:02:20,691
{\an8}Good for me. Well done.

32
00:02:25,154 --> 00:02:27,949
{\an8}I'll get out over there.
You get out at the main entrance.

33
00:02:28,324 --> 00:02:29,492
{\an8}No, it's fine.

34
00:02:30,326 --> 00:02:31,869
Let's just go straight to work.

35
00:02:33,329 --> 00:02:35,498
What's the occasion?
I don't mind this at all.

36
00:02:36,332 --> 00:02:37,416
Okay, then.

37
00:02:46,842 --> 00:02:47,843
Ms. Joo.

38
00:02:48,636 --> 00:02:49,637
Good morning.

39
00:02:51,305 --> 00:02:52,348
Hello.

40
00:02:57,478 --> 00:02:59,021
Did you get home safe last night?

41
00:03:00,523 --> 00:03:03,025
Oh, we had a team dinner.

42
00:03:06,279 --> 00:03:08,573
Yes, I got back just fine,
thanks to you.

43
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:11,325
- How do you feel...
- Ki-jun?

44
00:03:18,958 --> 00:03:20,042
What's this on you?

45
00:03:20,251 --> 00:03:22,545
You can't look disheveled
in front of your head.

46
00:03:23,754 --> 00:03:25,214
Don't you agree, Ms. Joo?

47
00:03:27,466 --> 00:03:29,844
Well,
I've already seen him disheveled.

48
00:03:38,311 --> 00:03:39,312
What was that about?

49
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:50,114
What do you think got into her?
Did she eat something weird?

50
00:03:50,615 --> 00:03:52,617
Did you hear about Mr. Do
from Haemu Cosmetics?

51
00:03:53,409 --> 00:03:54,619
Yes.

52
00:03:54,702 --> 00:03:56,662
I'll charge him with assault
and demoralizing behavior

53
00:03:56,746 --> 00:03:58,080
and apply for disciplinary action.

54
00:03:58,164 --> 00:03:59,624
A few of his client companies

55
00:03:59,707 --> 00:04:02,293
severed business ties
due to Mr. Do's actions.

56
00:04:02,376 --> 00:04:03,711
It's a sizable loss.

57
00:04:03,794 --> 00:04:05,588
Consult our Legal Team
and consider firing him, too.

58
00:04:06,213 --> 00:04:07,298
I'll do that.

59
00:04:08,466 --> 00:04:10,760
How do you feel, Ms. Joo?

60
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:12,637
Shouldn't you take a break?

61
00:04:13,512 --> 00:04:16,057
- How about taking the afternoon...
- I'm fine. I'm good.

62
00:04:16,307 --> 00:04:18,100
Could I have become
Haemu's youngest female executive

63
00:04:18,184 --> 00:04:20,728
if I had to take the afternoon
after just a few drinks?

64
00:04:21,312 --> 00:04:22,772
I'm Joo In-a.

65
00:04:23,022 --> 00:04:24,815
Something like that
will never make me...

66
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:32,323
I will never waver.

67
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,326
Got it.

68
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:38,871
Respect.

69
00:04:59,725 --> 00:05:02,144
Yes, looking good.

70
00:05:03,187 --> 00:05:04,814
The last frame.

71
00:05:07,817 --> 00:05:09,652
You're doing great, PK.

72
00:05:09,735 --> 00:05:11,987
The photos are amazing.

73
00:05:12,196 --> 00:05:14,865
- What time is it?
- It's a little after 9 p.m.

74
00:05:14,949 --> 00:05:17,368
What? Darn it.

75
00:05:18,369 --> 00:05:20,121
- I'm leaving.
- Where to?

76
00:05:20,454 --> 00:05:22,081
Sort things out for me.
She's waiting.

77
00:05:22,164 --> 00:05:25,000
We still have
a few more outfits to shoot.

78
00:05:25,292 --> 00:05:26,711
PK, where are you going?

79
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,152
What should we do later?

80
00:05:51,235 --> 00:05:52,319
What do you want to do?

81
00:05:53,446 --> 00:05:54,697
Don't get too jumpy.

82
00:05:55,114 --> 00:05:58,159
No, don't. I'm driving right now.

83
00:06:06,667 --> 00:06:08,210
- Hold back.
- What for?

84
00:06:08,294 --> 00:06:10,755
- We have lots of time.
- Kiss me.

85
00:06:10,838 --> 00:06:12,673
- Come on.
- I'm driving.

86
00:06:12,757 --> 00:06:14,133
- We stopped.
- Later.

87
00:06:14,216 --> 00:06:16,051
- No, I want it now.
- Wait.

88
00:06:16,135 --> 00:06:18,554
- Hang on. I really...
- No. Now.

89
00:06:21,682 --> 00:06:22,892
What the heck?

90
00:06:24,393 --> 00:06:25,394
Hey, you!

91
00:06:27,062 --> 00:06:29,690
- Who was that?
- You're dead meat.

92
00:06:35,112 --> 00:06:37,948
Step on it. He's getting away.

93
00:06:38,741 --> 00:06:40,034
He won't stop?

94
00:06:40,326 --> 00:06:42,161
This is so much fun.

95
00:06:52,296 --> 00:06:54,381
Keep going. Catch him.

96
00:06:54,799 --> 00:06:57,218
I want to drive, too.

97
00:06:57,301 --> 00:06:58,552
This is fun!

98
00:07:05,893 --> 00:07:07,353
Pull over!

99
00:07:07,686 --> 00:07:09,396
Who are you to take photos?

100
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,065
You! Pull over!

101
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:21,992
- Darn it.
- Shoot.

102
00:07:22,076 --> 00:07:23,661
We're done for.

103
00:07:24,036 --> 00:07:25,162
What happened?

104
00:07:25,371 --> 00:07:27,206
- Oh, my gosh.
- What the...

105
00:07:28,290 --> 00:07:29,708
I don't believe this.

106
00:07:30,167 --> 00:07:31,836
Are we done for?

107
00:07:32,336 --> 00:07:33,420
Come on out.

108
00:07:33,504 --> 00:07:35,923
- Shoot.
- We're screwed.

109
00:07:37,383 --> 00:07:39,468
<i>Top star singer and actor PK</i>

110
00:07:39,552 --> 00:07:43,889
<i>caused a traffic accident
in a main street late last night.</i>

111
00:07:43,973 --> 00:07:46,058
<i>Reports say it wasn't just a mistake.</i>

112
00:07:46,141 --> 00:07:49,854
<i>He gave chase and drove
into another car deliberately.</i>

113
00:07:49,937 --> 00:07:51,063
<i>Everyone's reeling in shock.</i>

114
00:07:51,146 --> 00:07:52,147
PK, A MIDNIGHT CHASE

115
00:07:52,231 --> 00:07:54,608
<i>Experts say PK
will have to pay a penalty</i>

116
00:07:54,692 --> 00:07:57,486
<i>reaching tens of billions of won
for his commercial deals.</i>

117
00:07:57,570 --> 00:07:59,905
<i>The industry is also in turmoil.</i>

118
00:07:59,989 --> 00:08:01,490
STRIVING FOR THE FUTURE

119
00:08:01,574 --> 00:08:03,951
Come on. PK.

120
00:08:04,702 --> 00:08:06,871
Why did you go and do that?

121
00:08:06,954 --> 00:08:08,873
With your handsome face.

122
00:08:12,835 --> 00:08:16,213
- You're a fan of PK?
- Yes, a die-hard fan.

123
00:08:16,547 --> 00:08:19,884
I used to collect PR material for her
if PK was on them.

124
00:08:23,971 --> 00:08:26,307
Does that mean
he's done being our company's model?

125
00:08:30,769 --> 00:08:32,479
- Mr. Moo.
- Yes?

126
00:08:32,563 --> 00:08:34,773
Can I go get a sugar boost?

127
00:08:35,190 --> 00:08:36,775
I have zero will to work right now.

128
00:08:36,859 --> 00:08:39,820
Yes, sure. Get some fresh
and gather yourself.

129
00:08:45,159 --> 00:08:48,454
Why would someone stan
a celebrity at that age?

130
00:08:49,288 --> 00:08:50,539
Don't you agree, Ms. Yoon?

131
00:08:50,623 --> 00:08:52,207
Some people are like that.

132
00:08:52,291 --> 00:08:54,585
Is there a star you like, Ms. Yoon?

133
00:08:54,668 --> 00:08:57,838
Do you think she's the type
to care about celebrities?

134
00:08:58,088 --> 00:09:00,716
She went to a prestigious university
and passed the accountant exam.

135
00:09:00,799 --> 00:09:02,885
- Oh, right.
- She did nothing but study

136
00:09:02,968 --> 00:09:05,262
with no distractions, right?

137
00:09:06,221 --> 00:09:08,515
Look. We're talking about her

138
00:09:08,599 --> 00:09:11,477
and she's concentrating on her work
without minding us.

139
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:13,604
- She'll be really successful.
- I'm jealous.

140
00:09:23,072 --> 00:09:24,865
NEW MESSAGE
FROM SHIN JI-HYE OF MARKETING

141
00:09:27,368 --> 00:09:29,244
<i>Ki-jun, are you busy?</i>

142
00:09:32,039 --> 00:09:34,500
The wedding invitation looks great.
Congratulations.

143
00:09:35,584 --> 00:09:36,627
Thanks.

144
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,838
Ki-jun, the thing is...

145
00:09:40,673 --> 00:09:42,383
I want to apologize.

146
00:09:43,842 --> 00:09:47,054
For what I did to you
in the stairwell.

147
00:09:47,805 --> 00:09:49,473
I came onto you.

148
00:09:52,851 --> 00:09:55,062
Maybe I have wedding jitters,
like you said.

149
00:09:55,145 --> 00:09:58,023
I've learned my lesson
and turned over a new leaf.

150
00:09:58,399 --> 00:10:00,067
I'll be true and loyal to my husband.

151
00:10:00,150 --> 00:10:02,152
Good. You made the right call.

152
00:10:02,236 --> 00:10:03,362
Live happily ever after.

153
00:10:05,406 --> 00:10:06,865
How are the preparations going?

154
00:10:07,533 --> 00:10:09,410
I'm more worried about my workload.

155
00:10:09,493 --> 00:10:10,995
I hope I'll be done
before the wedding.

156
00:10:11,662 --> 00:10:14,957
Oh, it's because PK messed up, right?

157
00:10:15,666 --> 00:10:18,210
Finding another company model
will be a lot of work.

158
00:10:18,585 --> 00:10:21,338
No, we're not replacing him.

159
00:10:21,422 --> 00:10:23,507
- You're not?
- My team leader put it on hold.

160
00:10:24,049 --> 00:10:26,760
The investigation's still underway,
so she wants to wait.

161
00:10:26,844 --> 00:10:29,430
Why wait?
Isn't a model all about image?

162
00:10:29,888 --> 00:10:31,015
I can't say.

163
00:10:31,724 --> 00:10:34,101
PK is still huge abroad.

164
00:10:35,686 --> 00:10:38,605
To be honest, I don't get it, either.

165
00:10:39,273 --> 00:10:40,566
Does PK have connections?

166
00:10:41,442 --> 00:10:42,568
You think so?

167
00:10:51,035 --> 00:10:52,536
Congrats anyway.
See you at the wedding.

168
00:10:52,619 --> 00:10:53,620
Okay.

169
00:10:55,205 --> 00:10:57,499
Ms. Joo,
did you have a meeting elsewhere?

170
00:10:58,167 --> 00:10:59,877
You must have no work to do.

171
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:03,047
Do you have time to enjoy
a coffee break during work hours?

172
00:11:03,130 --> 00:11:05,549
That's how I gather information.

173
00:11:05,883 --> 00:11:07,968
I think I got something big.

174
00:11:08,052 --> 00:11:09,970
I'm not sure if it's a PM case

175
00:11:10,054 --> 00:11:12,181
but my experience tells me
there's more to it.

176
00:11:14,433 --> 00:11:15,434
What is it about?

177
00:11:18,187 --> 00:11:19,313
You know PK, right?

178
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:29,531
<i>These are all the files
on our company model contracts</i>

179
00:11:29,615 --> 00:11:30,991
<i>going back five years.</i>

180
00:11:34,036 --> 00:11:36,288
Not just signed contracts
but step-by-step reports

181
00:11:36,371 --> 00:11:38,040
minutes, internal memos, invoices

182
00:11:38,123 --> 00:11:41,085
emails that went to and fro
are right here.

183
00:11:41,376 --> 00:11:44,004
Read everything thoroughly
and check for discrepancies.

184
00:11:45,547 --> 00:11:49,635
- I only wanted to look into PK...
- You have a prejudice about him.

185
00:11:49,718 --> 00:11:52,012
That could
make this investigation biased.

186
00:11:52,846 --> 00:11:54,640
And we should compare PK's deal

187
00:11:54,723 --> 00:11:56,809
with that of other models'
to find out if there's a problem.

188
00:11:57,059 --> 00:11:58,102
Right?

189
00:11:58,477 --> 00:12:00,813
Let's get it done ASAP.

190
00:12:14,451 --> 00:12:16,912
How many times must I say I won't go?

191
00:12:17,496 --> 00:12:20,332
Why should I go just to watch
some old folk brag?

192
00:12:20,415 --> 00:12:22,126
I told you about it for a whole month

193
00:12:22,209 --> 00:12:24,711
that it's an important event
and you shouldn't drink before going.

194
00:12:25,921 --> 00:12:27,172
So what?

195
00:12:27,548 --> 00:12:29,091
I'm drinking already.

196
00:12:34,888 --> 00:12:36,807
You're an alcoholic.

197
00:12:37,558 --> 00:12:38,600
You need help.

198
00:12:45,858 --> 00:12:47,317
Sorry for laughing.

199
00:12:52,865 --> 00:12:54,032
What?

200
00:12:56,702 --> 00:12:57,786
Are you afraid?

201
00:12:59,121 --> 00:13:01,290
That I'll go crazy like your mom?

202
00:13:08,547 --> 00:13:09,590
Hey.

203
00:13:12,009 --> 00:13:13,802
I told you not to give me that look.

204
00:13:18,432 --> 00:13:20,350
Don't look at me like that!

205
00:13:53,217 --> 00:13:55,135
- Ms. Han.
- Yes?

206
00:13:55,219 --> 00:13:56,929
Are you not picking up
your kids today?

207
00:13:57,012 --> 00:14:00,057
I should leave soon. You go ahead.

208
00:14:01,934 --> 00:14:03,310
Weddings are hard to plan, right?

209
00:14:03,393 --> 00:14:05,270
There's so much to do.

210
00:14:05,354 --> 00:14:07,189
Tell me if you need help
with anything.

211
00:14:07,272 --> 00:14:09,650
- I will. Thank you.
- Go on home.

212
00:14:11,401 --> 00:14:13,820
- See you tomorrow.
- Bye.

213
00:15:01,034 --> 00:15:02,536
What took you so long?

214
00:15:02,619 --> 00:15:04,955
Come here.
You kept me waiting a while.

215
00:15:15,799 --> 00:15:17,843
Why are you going back inside?
Do you have to stay late?

216
00:15:24,141 --> 00:15:25,767
Why do you
keep talking to me at work?

217
00:15:25,851 --> 00:15:27,477
You used to want me to stay away.

218
00:15:27,894 --> 00:15:29,855
And why did you fix my tie yesterday

219
00:15:29,938 --> 00:15:31,732
in front of Ms. Joo in the elevator?

220
00:15:31,815 --> 00:15:33,275
You gave me a real scare.

221
00:15:33,358 --> 00:15:35,902
Why are you overreacting?

222
00:15:36,278 --> 00:15:38,572
Is there a reason
Joo In-a can't know?

223
00:15:38,655 --> 00:15:39,656
About us?

224
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:42,701
No, I'm saying
we should be careful around everyone.

225
00:15:43,285 --> 00:15:44,328
Too bad.

226
00:15:45,329 --> 00:15:47,080
Joo In-a knows already.

227
00:15:49,291 --> 00:15:52,044
That we're living together.

228
00:15:54,254 --> 00:15:56,256
- What do you mean?
- Two days ago.

229
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:59,176
She brought you home
the night you got drunk.

230
00:15:59,259 --> 00:16:00,302
What?

231
00:16:03,472 --> 00:16:04,848
Why are you telling me that now?

232
00:16:04,931 --> 00:16:07,684
I didn't know
it meant so much to you.

233
00:16:11,313 --> 00:16:13,231
Did you tell her
that there's nothing between us?

234
00:16:13,315 --> 00:16:14,691
I told her exactly how things are.

235
00:16:15,901 --> 00:16:17,110
That we used to date.

236
00:16:33,251 --> 00:16:34,419
What's her problem?

237
00:16:59,903 --> 00:17:01,071
Ms. Joo.

238
00:17:01,738 --> 00:17:03,073
Didn't you go home?

239
00:17:03,156 --> 00:17:05,659
I came back
for something I'd forgotten.

240
00:17:05,992 --> 00:17:07,369
Are you finished with this pile?

241
00:17:07,452 --> 00:17:09,162
I don't mind working on it alone.

242
00:17:09,246 --> 00:17:11,373
Let's not waste company funds
on too much overtime.

243
00:17:24,177 --> 00:17:25,429
Did you have dinner?

244
00:17:26,430 --> 00:17:27,431
Would you like to have this?

245
00:17:28,265 --> 00:17:29,266
No.

246
00:17:30,142 --> 00:17:31,143
Okay.

247
00:17:42,821 --> 00:17:45,991
I heard you took me home.

248
00:17:46,575 --> 00:17:49,161
Yes, you should lose some weight.

249
00:17:50,745 --> 00:17:54,124
I weigh more than I look
because I'm pure muscle.

250
00:18:05,802 --> 00:18:08,221
Ms. Park and I are just friends.

251
00:18:08,805 --> 00:18:10,265
We have in separate rooms

252
00:18:10,348 --> 00:18:12,434
and we barely meet at home
because we're both so busy.

253
00:18:12,726 --> 00:18:15,353
Our arrangement
is more like what housemates...

254
00:18:15,437 --> 00:18:16,480
Mr. Noh.

255
00:18:16,563 --> 00:18:18,607
You don't have to explain that to me.

256
00:18:19,733 --> 00:18:21,026
It's your private life.

257
00:18:26,490 --> 00:18:28,283
Don't you care about my private life?

258
00:18:29,367 --> 00:18:30,494
We even kissed.

259
00:18:34,623 --> 00:18:35,790
I don't care.

260
00:18:36,249 --> 00:18:37,584
And don't you care about me.

261
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:39,377
Didn't we agree to be cool about it?

262
00:18:40,378 --> 00:18:41,755
Then will you

263
00:18:42,881 --> 00:18:44,382
answer my question...

264
00:18:46,885 --> 00:18:48,803
why you push me away.

265
00:18:55,602 --> 00:18:58,146
You asked if I was seeing someone.

266
00:18:59,272 --> 00:19:01,024
Isn't that too personal a question?

267
00:19:01,816 --> 00:19:03,318
We're at work.

268
00:19:03,401 --> 00:19:06,321
Let's stop talking about that
and stick to work-related stuff.

269
00:19:06,404 --> 00:19:08,198
What if it is work-related?

270
00:19:11,493 --> 00:19:12,661
What does that mean?

271
00:19:14,371 --> 00:19:17,040
Can my love life be work-related?

272
00:19:17,123 --> 00:19:18,208
It can.

273
00:19:18,875 --> 00:19:20,794
Depending on who you date.

274
00:19:52,284 --> 00:19:53,910
He didn't come home.

275
00:19:54,995 --> 00:19:56,955
PROPOSAL: COMPANY MODEL

276
00:21:22,791 --> 00:21:25,418
It's definitely suspicious,
even if I look at it without bias.

277
00:21:25,502 --> 00:21:28,463
Haemu first signed PK
as the company model in 2020.

278
00:21:28,546 --> 00:21:30,632
He was unknown then,
and we paid him 300 million won.

279
00:21:32,967 --> 00:21:35,470
When he resigned in 2021,
the pay soared to one billion won.

280
00:21:35,553 --> 00:21:36,888
ONE BILLION KOREAN WON

281
00:21:37,597 --> 00:21:40,392
I don't see why that's a problem.
He soared to stardom in that year.

282
00:21:40,475 --> 00:21:42,852
Almost any model in his caliber
would be paid that much

283
00:21:42,936 --> 00:21:44,979
- and we demanded a lot of him.
- Yes.

284
00:21:45,271 --> 00:21:46,481
You're right about that much.

285
00:21:48,566 --> 00:21:51,152
But then he's criticized
for poor acting

286
00:21:51,236 --> 00:21:54,030
and excessive commercial use
of his image, diminishing his value.

287
00:21:55,031 --> 00:21:56,950
And still, we renew his contract
for five billion won.

288
00:21:57,575 --> 00:21:59,994
And this deal is for three years,
not the customary one year.

289
00:22:00,495 --> 00:22:03,206
I don't think
we were taken advantage of.

290
00:22:03,665 --> 00:22:06,418
It makes me think he has dirt on us.

291
00:22:09,254 --> 00:22:10,588
But guess what the weirdest thing is.

292
00:22:11,172 --> 00:22:13,174
Around the time
we must decide on a model

293
00:22:13,258 --> 00:22:15,802
Marketing communicates immensely
internally and with agencies

294
00:22:15,885 --> 00:22:18,054
to discuss possible models

295
00:22:18,138 --> 00:22:20,432
and to iron out demands
and requirements.

296
00:22:20,515 --> 00:22:21,683
But when it comes to PK

297
00:22:22,559 --> 00:22:23,727
they did nothing of the sort.

298
00:22:24,394 --> 00:22:26,521
They didn't go to his agency once

299
00:22:26,604 --> 00:22:29,065
and they didn't even correspond
via email.

300
00:22:30,108 --> 00:22:31,985
If what should be there is missing

301
00:22:32,068 --> 00:22:34,988
it can mean something
that shouldn't have been there was.

302
00:22:35,488 --> 00:22:36,573
Yes.

303
00:22:38,783 --> 00:22:39,909
The problem is

304
00:22:40,535 --> 00:22:42,620
how do we prove that?

305
00:22:42,704 --> 00:22:44,164
While you were studying the documents

306
00:22:44,247 --> 00:22:47,417
I went through
PK's social media posts.

307
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:48,501
What?

308
00:22:49,878 --> 00:22:51,087
You had all the fun.

309
00:22:51,671 --> 00:22:52,964
This must've been fun.

310
00:22:53,798 --> 00:22:55,759
It wasn't. My eyes hurt like crazy.

311
00:22:56,259 --> 00:22:57,802
Don't you see how they're bloodshot?

312
00:22:57,886 --> 00:22:58,928
Where?

313
00:23:12,275 --> 00:23:13,526
Anyway.

314
00:23:13,902 --> 00:23:16,529
PK posted something in March 2020.

315
00:23:18,740 --> 00:23:19,866
It's this photo.

316
00:23:20,116 --> 00:23:21,868
It looked expensively luxurious

317
00:23:22,285 --> 00:23:24,621
so I zoomed in on this window
and looked it up.

318
00:23:25,205 --> 00:23:29,334
It's a crazy expensive
private hot spring in Osaka, Japan.

319
00:23:29,959 --> 00:23:32,629
He's a celebrity, so he would
go on a date at a place like this.

320
00:23:33,129 --> 00:23:34,214
Right.

321
00:23:36,216 --> 00:23:37,967
At around this time

322
00:23:38,218 --> 00:23:40,345
this exact same period

323
00:23:41,054 --> 00:23:43,389
there's a Haemu employee
who used their company card in Osaka.

324
00:23:44,516 --> 00:23:46,267
The transaction
was canceled right away

325
00:23:46,351 --> 00:23:49,729
but I can't say if it was because
she felt a pang of guilt

326
00:23:49,813 --> 00:23:51,648
or because she wanted
to erase her trace.

327
00:23:53,650 --> 00:23:58,029
But Osaka is one of the places
where Koreans love to visit.

328
00:23:58,780 --> 00:24:01,115
It could just be a coincidence.

329
00:24:02,826 --> 00:24:04,202
What if that employee

330
00:24:06,996 --> 00:24:08,540
had the final say in signing PK?

331
00:24:09,999 --> 00:24:11,334
Doesn't that change everything?

332
00:24:15,088 --> 00:24:17,215
TEAM LEADER HAN JI-WON

333
00:24:25,715 --> 00:24:27,008
Are you a slow reader?

334
00:24:27,592 --> 00:24:29,302
You're taking way too long.

335
00:24:31,346 --> 00:24:32,931
COMPANY MODEL: PK
STANDARD CONTRACT

336
00:24:33,348 --> 00:24:35,267
It's okay. Take your time.

337
00:24:35,934 --> 00:24:37,102
Thank you.

338
00:24:44,818 --> 00:24:47,821
We follow the due process
when selecting a company model.

339
00:24:48,655 --> 00:24:50,490
But in PK's case

340
00:24:50,574 --> 00:24:52,659
we've had a long-standing
model-client relationship

341
00:24:52,742 --> 00:24:54,578
and I guess that's why
things were a bit lax.

342
00:24:55,036 --> 00:24:56,037
What about the Japan trip?

343
00:24:56,872 --> 00:24:58,331
That was pure coincidence.

344
00:24:58,999 --> 00:25:02,085
I went there on a family trip
with my two kids and husband.

345
00:25:03,003 --> 00:25:04,337
I used the wrong credit card.

346
00:25:04,921 --> 00:25:08,633
I used it at a convenience store,
but I canceled it right away.

347
00:25:10,218 --> 00:25:11,803
You went with your family.

348
00:25:12,512 --> 00:25:14,556
Can I see the photos you took?

349
00:25:15,891 --> 00:25:19,394
I'd love to show you,
but I got a new phone recently.

350
00:25:19,644 --> 00:25:21,229
I don't have any of the photos.

351
00:25:21,313 --> 00:25:22,397
Oh, dear.

352
00:25:22,481 --> 00:25:24,441
You lost all the photos of your kids?

353
00:25:24,774 --> 00:25:26,026
You didn't save them
to a cloud server?

354
00:25:27,277 --> 00:25:29,571
I didn't. I'm not that good
with technology.

355
00:25:30,155 --> 00:25:31,698
Let's see your phone.

356
00:25:32,032 --> 00:25:33,533
- What?
- I don't believe you.

357
00:25:33,617 --> 00:25:35,076
Let me see your phone.

358
00:25:35,994 --> 00:25:39,206
Do I have to show you my phone?

359
00:25:39,289 --> 00:25:40,749
It's our due process.

360
00:25:41,416 --> 00:25:43,502
You'll sign a consent form
before handing it over.

361
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:46,755
Of course,
you can refuse to turn it in.

362
00:25:47,589 --> 00:25:50,300
But that won't do you any good.

363
00:25:53,595 --> 00:25:55,430
It wasn't a family trip.

364
00:25:55,722 --> 00:25:58,934
What Korean mom
takes her kids to a hot spring

365
00:25:59,017 --> 00:26:02,312
in Japan in March, the month
her first kid starts school?

366
00:26:02,646 --> 00:26:04,648
We know your husband didn't travel.

367
00:26:05,273 --> 00:26:06,650
We confirmed it already.

368
00:26:23,625 --> 00:26:24,751
We're dating.

369
00:26:27,337 --> 00:26:28,463
PK and I.

370
00:26:31,216 --> 00:26:32,425
We're lovers.

371
00:26:43,270 --> 00:26:45,397
Ms. Han gave in too easily.

372
00:26:46,231 --> 00:26:48,316
I interviewed her coworkers
beforehand

373
00:26:48,900 --> 00:26:50,735
and they said
she was stubborn and uptight.

374
00:26:51,444 --> 00:26:53,530
I even prepared a few more scenarios
to use against her.

375
00:26:55,448 --> 00:26:56,449
Are you busy today?

376
00:27:12,424 --> 00:27:13,508
Oh, dear.

377
00:27:30,567 --> 00:27:33,194
Min-yul, sit up straight
and wear your seat belt.

378
00:27:33,278 --> 00:27:34,404
It's my turn now.

379
00:27:35,739 --> 00:27:37,282
- I got it.
- You're done for the day?

380
00:27:37,365 --> 00:27:39,784
Come on. Give it back to me.

381
00:27:39,868 --> 00:27:41,953
You won't even say hi to Mom.

382
00:27:44,205 --> 00:27:45,874
Don't run, boys.

383
00:27:47,626 --> 00:27:48,960
Dong-yun, turn that off.

384
00:27:49,461 --> 00:27:51,796
Honey, I'm so very sorry.

385
00:27:52,047 --> 00:27:54,716
I barely shut down my boss
who wanted to go for round two.

386
00:27:54,799 --> 00:27:57,135
- Good for you.
- Dong-yun, you won't even say hi?

387
00:27:59,888 --> 00:28:01,556
Don't you love dumplings?

388
00:28:01,931 --> 00:28:04,059
Can we have some? Try one.

389
00:28:04,142 --> 00:28:05,810
- Leave it.
- Come on.

390
00:28:05,894 --> 00:28:07,395
- Don't be silly.
- Open wide.

391
00:28:09,981 --> 00:28:12,275
They seem to be happily married.

392
00:28:12,359 --> 00:28:13,610
Yes.

393
00:28:13,693 --> 00:28:16,154
- Isn't she too busy to have a lover?
- We'll take a pack.

394
00:28:17,197 --> 00:28:18,990
Thank you. Bye.

395
00:28:21,076 --> 00:28:23,411
Lee Dong-yun.
Quit playing on that phone.

396
00:28:26,164 --> 00:28:28,166
Yes, that one, maybe.

397
00:28:41,429 --> 00:28:43,348
Is Ms. Han really PK's lover?

398
00:28:43,431 --> 00:28:44,849
Is that why she favored him?

399
00:28:44,933 --> 00:28:47,102
Is this the sponsor thing
I'd only heard about?

400
00:28:47,185 --> 00:28:49,229
Where would she get the money for it?

401
00:28:49,312 --> 00:28:51,773
Does she make much more than I
when I'm also a team leader?

402
00:28:51,856 --> 00:28:53,316
- No.
- He said

403
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:55,860
he was too busy with work to date

404
00:28:55,944 --> 00:28:59,030
and he acted all sweet and naive,
like he only cared for his fans.

405
00:28:59,739 --> 00:29:02,742
I didn't believe every word he said

406
00:29:02,826 --> 00:29:04,536
but isn't this just wrong?

407
00:29:04,869 --> 00:29:08,748
How could he sleep around
with a married mom of three?

408
00:29:09,290 --> 00:29:11,918
The second-hand embarrassment
is killing me.

409
00:29:19,175 --> 00:29:20,802
- What's wrong?
- What are you doing?

410
00:29:21,761 --> 00:29:23,680
Why are you suddenly
cleaning out your drawer?

411
00:29:25,598 --> 00:29:27,016
- What...
- Why...

412
00:29:28,268 --> 00:29:29,477
What's wrong?

413
00:29:30,103 --> 00:29:32,188
- Why the sudden outburst?
- This is...

414
00:29:34,607 --> 00:29:35,942
It's PK's merchandise.

415
00:29:37,444 --> 00:29:39,863
<i>No one can confirm who was in his car</i>

416
00:29:40,155 --> 00:29:42,657
at the time of the accident?

417
00:29:43,450 --> 00:29:45,410
That's right.
No one has any information.

418
00:29:45,493 --> 00:29:47,120
Even the reporters
are getting frustrated.

419
00:29:48,037 --> 00:29:50,707
If Ms. Han is telling a lie...

420
00:29:51,833 --> 00:29:54,294
Why on earth? It would get her fired.

421
00:29:55,378 --> 00:29:58,089
Could there be something
she fears more than losing her job?

422
00:30:04,721 --> 00:30:06,806
I told you
not to over-water the plant.

423
00:30:09,267 --> 00:30:11,019
You told me?

424
00:30:12,479 --> 00:30:13,897
I'm your superior.

425
00:30:17,650 --> 00:30:19,652
It's better to be straightforward.

426
00:30:21,654 --> 00:30:22,781
Put that down.

427
00:30:28,787 --> 00:30:30,205
It doesn't feel right

428
00:30:31,039 --> 00:30:33,124
that Ms. Han is PK's lover.

429
00:30:33,500 --> 00:30:35,251
The women PK dated so far

430
00:30:35,335 --> 00:30:37,337
are idol singer Ha Jeong-yun,
actress Yang Hee-seung

431
00:30:37,420 --> 00:30:39,672
hotel heiress Jo Moon-joo,
and influencer Lee Ji-hyun.

432
00:30:39,756 --> 00:30:41,466
They're all puppy-faced girls

433
00:30:41,549 --> 00:30:44,093
who are relatively short and cute.

434
00:30:44,177 --> 00:30:46,763
But Ms. Han's awfully tall

435
00:30:46,846 --> 00:30:48,306
and she has cat-like features.

436
00:30:49,182 --> 00:30:50,391
Not to mention she's married.

437
00:30:51,476 --> 00:30:53,102
She's not even rich enough
to be a sponsor.

438
00:30:53,770 --> 00:30:55,855
Gosh, Ms. Yoon.

439
00:30:56,606 --> 00:30:58,900
You seem to know a great deal
about PK.

440
00:31:01,277 --> 00:31:02,445
I used to be a fan.

441
00:31:03,655 --> 00:31:04,989
I quit just now.

442
00:31:07,242 --> 00:31:09,452
You must've been a die-hard fan.

443
00:31:10,829 --> 00:31:11,830
Do you know

444
00:31:12,914 --> 00:31:14,207
where to look?

445
00:31:14,791 --> 00:31:17,252
How about rumors among real fans?

446
00:31:18,127 --> 00:31:19,128
Or how about

447
00:31:19,712 --> 00:31:21,506
social media posts about PK?

448
00:31:26,970 --> 00:31:29,305
There's a well-known PK stalker fan

449
00:31:29,889 --> 00:31:31,474
that all the other fans know about.

450
00:31:32,892 --> 00:31:35,812
<i>He said he had photos
from the scene of the accident.</i>

451
00:31:36,104 --> 00:31:38,273
<i>He made a threatening post.</i>

452
00:31:38,356 --> 00:31:40,233
WE'LL PROTECT YOU, PK
STAY STRONG, PK

453
00:31:41,067 --> 00:31:42,986
<i>He might know something.</i>

454
00:31:46,114 --> 00:31:47,365
STAY STRONG, PK
WE'RE BY YOUR SIDE

455
00:31:58,960 --> 00:32:00,920
Are you PK Rabbit?

456
00:32:01,004 --> 00:32:02,797
I recognized your rabbit ears.

457
00:32:02,881 --> 00:32:04,132
They're adorable.

458
00:32:06,551 --> 00:32:07,552
Yikes.

459
00:32:14,100 --> 00:32:16,811
I'm the person who sent you the DM.

460
00:32:18,354 --> 00:32:19,981
I wanted to buy a photo card.

461
00:32:20,481 --> 00:32:22,108
Are you really here for a photo card?

462
00:32:23,109 --> 00:32:25,403
Aren't you from some large company?

463
00:32:27,196 --> 00:32:29,157
I am from a large company,
but how do you know...

464
00:32:31,826 --> 00:32:33,578
Why? What do you want?

465
00:32:34,746 --> 00:32:37,373
What's the matter? What's this about?

466
00:32:47,717 --> 00:32:50,428
The photos I gave you last time
were all I had.

467
00:32:51,012 --> 00:32:52,513
I didn't make any copies.

468
00:32:53,056 --> 00:32:54,891
- And please, mister.
- Yes, what?

469
00:32:54,974 --> 00:32:56,142
I'll quit being a fan.

470
00:32:56,225 --> 00:32:58,519
I won't take any more photos

471
00:32:58,603 --> 00:33:00,313
and I won't follow PK around anymore.

472
00:33:00,730 --> 00:33:05,151
- What's this about? Get up.
- So please, leave me alone.

473
00:33:05,860 --> 00:33:09,822
- I'm not...
- Your company is bullying people!

474
00:33:23,878 --> 00:33:26,047
What company are you talking about?

475
00:33:29,384 --> 00:33:34,263
Aren't you from Sesan Group?

476
00:33:35,974 --> 00:33:37,183
Sesan Group?

477
00:33:39,727 --> 00:33:41,270
These are the originals.

478
00:33:41,688 --> 00:33:43,356
I confirmed there are no copies.

479
00:33:51,906 --> 00:33:53,032
Good job.

480
00:33:55,076 --> 00:33:56,160
Nice one.

481
00:34:02,041 --> 00:34:06,462
Did you really say
you and I were dating?

482
00:34:08,548 --> 00:34:10,425
Did they believe that?

483
00:34:11,551 --> 00:34:12,927
What idiots.

484
00:34:15,680 --> 00:34:17,682
I'll post your husband to Europe.

485
00:34:18,433 --> 00:34:19,642
Flee quietly.

486
00:34:41,956 --> 00:34:44,167
As people say, former fans
can be the scariest haters.

487
00:34:47,003 --> 00:34:48,254
Anyway.

488
00:34:48,629 --> 00:34:50,798
I've been a PK stan for years
while you worked with me.

489
00:34:50,882 --> 00:34:52,759
How come
you never even brought it up?

490
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:54,761
Gosh.

491
00:34:56,471 --> 00:34:57,513
Ms. Yoon.

492
00:34:58,347 --> 00:35:00,850
I know you aren't looking
to make friends at work

493
00:35:01,768 --> 00:35:03,352
but this one was too harsh.

494
00:35:12,987 --> 00:35:14,655
Isn't this
the exclusive fan club merch?

495
00:35:15,448 --> 00:35:16,824
And it's the first generation.

496
00:35:18,159 --> 00:35:21,579
The resale price for this is crazy.
Why did you throw it out?

497
00:35:21,662 --> 00:35:22,705
That benefits no one.

498
00:35:22,789 --> 00:35:25,041
At least sell it and eat
some <i>tteokbokki </i>with the money.

499
00:35:29,712 --> 00:35:30,755
Well.

500
00:35:31,172 --> 00:35:33,007
I can treat you today.

501
00:35:34,050 --> 00:35:35,468
I sold a few things already.

502
00:35:36,469 --> 00:35:37,720
I'm rich now.

503
00:35:47,063 --> 00:35:48,356
I can never say

504
00:35:50,650 --> 00:35:51,734
no to <i>tteokbokki</i>.

505
00:35:54,237 --> 00:35:55,238
Let's go.

506
00:35:57,115 --> 00:35:58,699
Wait up, Ms. Yoon.

507
00:35:59,492 --> 00:36:02,036
How do you like your <i>tteokbokki?</i>
Made with flour or rice?

508
00:36:02,120 --> 00:36:03,162
I'm a rice girl.

509
00:36:04,622 --> 00:36:06,791
What is it? Tell me.

510
00:36:07,083 --> 00:36:09,335
It seems like you and I have
the same taste in things.

511
00:36:10,461 --> 00:36:12,463
I told you
to carry the ball with you.

512
00:36:12,547 --> 00:36:13,756
You're going to hurt people.

513
00:36:14,423 --> 00:36:16,217
Min-yul! Goodness.

514
00:36:23,307 --> 00:36:24,392
So?

515
00:36:25,518 --> 00:36:26,519
Are you any good at soccer?

516
00:36:29,480 --> 00:36:30,606
Hey.

517
00:36:30,731 --> 00:36:32,233
Go out! And shoot!

518
00:36:32,316 --> 00:36:33,693
Hey, wait!

519
00:36:34,110 --> 00:36:35,903
- Start running.
- Wait for me!

520
00:36:35,987 --> 00:36:37,238
Get the ball!

521
00:36:37,905 --> 00:36:40,199
- Here!
- What are you doing?

522
00:36:40,283 --> 00:36:41,951
What are you doing, man?

523
00:36:45,746 --> 00:36:48,583
Hey, this is cheating!

524
00:36:48,666 --> 00:36:50,042
Stop! I said, stop!

525
00:36:51,252 --> 00:36:52,628
Stand in a line right here.

526
00:36:53,045 --> 00:36:55,715
You aren't supposed
to play dirty, boys.

527
00:36:55,798 --> 00:36:56,924
Play fair.

528
00:36:57,717 --> 00:36:58,926
Isn't that right, Mommy?

529
00:37:02,471 --> 00:37:04,682
Now, go out and play!

530
00:37:05,850 --> 00:37:08,311
- I got it.
- Hey, you can't play alone!

531
00:37:08,394 --> 00:37:09,562
- Wait!
- I'm so tired.

532
00:37:18,446 --> 00:37:20,990
You raise three boys and yet,
you're the Marketing Team Lead.

533
00:37:21,240 --> 00:37:22,825
You're something, Ms. Han.

534
00:37:26,412 --> 00:37:27,872
Plus, you have a guy on the side.

535
00:37:29,498 --> 00:37:30,708
Aren't you going on a date today?

536
00:37:34,587 --> 00:37:36,964
Your husband works
for Sesan Group, doesn't he?

537
00:37:39,634 --> 00:37:41,761
That must've become your weakness.

538
00:37:42,011 --> 00:37:43,346
She doesn't have any power over us

539
00:37:43,930 --> 00:37:46,224
but her influence
can't be ignored at Sesan.

540
00:37:56,817 --> 00:37:58,611
It looks like
you already know everything.

541
00:37:59,904 --> 00:38:01,239
What's your plan now?

542
00:38:02,573 --> 00:38:03,616
What did she say?

543
00:38:03,699 --> 00:38:05,034
We were told to move abroad.

544
00:38:05,576 --> 00:38:07,370
She'll post my husband overseas.

545
00:38:08,537 --> 00:38:09,830
Once I disappear

546
00:38:10,706 --> 00:38:13,084
the case will dissolve because
the person responsible isn't around

547
00:38:13,584 --> 00:38:15,294
and PK will continue to model for us.

548
00:38:17,296 --> 00:38:19,131
Those two will
continue to have an affair

549
00:38:19,215 --> 00:38:20,466
while only you're known as a woman

550
00:38:21,509 --> 00:38:22,927
who slept with a celebrity,
gave him a gig

551
00:38:23,010 --> 00:38:24,929
and then fled abroad
once you got caught?

552
00:38:26,847 --> 00:38:28,975
You're going to be a legend.

553
00:38:31,060 --> 00:38:33,896
So 15 years of diligent service
since the day you began at age 25

554
00:38:34,605 --> 00:38:35,648
comes to nothing?

555
00:38:37,525 --> 00:38:40,319
Well, that kind of rumor
is probably not the worst.

556
00:38:41,654 --> 00:38:43,781
I told your sons
that I was your friend from work.

557
00:38:44,365 --> 00:38:46,117
That kid is Min-uk,
your second son, right?

558
00:38:46,409 --> 00:38:47,702
He asked me

559
00:38:48,411 --> 00:38:49,787
if I were the captain's friend.

560
00:38:50,204 --> 00:38:52,206
He said his mother
was the captain at work

561
00:38:53,708 --> 00:38:56,752
so I should listen to you
and never cause any trouble.

562
00:38:57,878 --> 00:39:00,589
What a caring son you have.
He should be more obedient.

563
00:39:00,673 --> 00:39:01,674
Don't you think?

564
00:39:02,717 --> 00:39:05,094
I told him that I was a team leader,
not a captain.

565
00:39:11,017 --> 00:39:12,059
Do you want help?

566
00:39:17,273 --> 00:39:19,900
I'm a pretty useful shield, actually.

567
00:39:21,986 --> 00:39:23,112
Don't you want to use me?

568
00:39:23,904 --> 00:39:26,490
I promised the boys
that I'd keep the captain safe.

569
00:39:40,629 --> 00:39:41,756
All right.

570
00:39:41,839 --> 00:39:44,008
I'm good now. I've resurrected.

571
00:39:44,717 --> 00:39:46,719
- Come at me again.
- Okay!

572
00:40:06,906 --> 00:40:09,283
- Wait! It's my ball!
- No, it's mine!

573
00:40:09,367 --> 00:40:11,035
Pass it behind you.

574
00:40:11,118 --> 00:40:13,371
Over here! Pass it to me.

575
00:40:16,040 --> 00:40:18,751
Thus, the fundamental issue here is

576
00:40:18,834 --> 00:40:22,213
that Ms. A could pressure Marketing
into showing favor to the model Mr. B

577
00:40:22,296 --> 00:40:24,632
because of the system we created
for advertisement production.

578
00:40:26,258 --> 00:40:29,053
Hence, we propose a measure
to reinforce transparency in the...

579
00:40:29,136 --> 00:40:30,471
Hey, wait a second.

580
00:40:32,098 --> 00:40:33,224
I mean, please.

581
00:40:33,641 --> 00:40:34,892
Who's Ms. A?

582
00:40:34,975 --> 00:40:36,936
I get that Mr. B, the model, is PK.

583
00:40:37,019 --> 00:40:39,939
You have to tell us who Ms. A is.
We're dying to know who it is.

584
00:40:40,022 --> 00:40:41,649
That's not the point of the issue.

585
00:40:41,732 --> 00:40:43,859
Bringing up the actual name
may be considered libel.

586
00:40:43,943 --> 00:40:46,612
Come on. We aren't strangers here.

587
00:40:46,695 --> 00:40:48,572
Libel? Don't make me sad.

588
00:40:48,656 --> 00:40:51,367
We apologize that we could not share
every aspect of the case.

589
00:40:52,034 --> 00:40:54,120
However,
once Ms. A's identity is disclosed

590
00:40:54,412 --> 00:40:57,081
it may create a bigger business risk.

591
00:40:57,456 --> 00:40:59,125
I appreciate your understanding.

592
00:40:59,291 --> 00:41:03,337
Who in the world is it?

593
00:41:07,258 --> 00:41:08,300
Hyun-young.

594
00:41:08,843 --> 00:41:10,344
What brings you here?

595
00:41:18,018 --> 00:41:19,395
Who's Joo In-a?

596
00:41:38,622 --> 00:41:40,499
Who do you think you are to fire PK?

597
00:41:40,833 --> 00:41:42,585
Who do you think you are, you wench?

598
00:41:42,668 --> 00:41:45,880
How dare you fire him?
Who do you think you are?

599
00:41:51,093 --> 00:41:53,262
What are you doing? Let go.

600
00:41:54,305 --> 00:41:55,431
Let go!

601
00:41:56,056 --> 00:41:57,266
I said, let go!

602
00:42:08,986 --> 00:42:11,906
Hey, Jeon Jae-yeol.
Have you lost your mind?

603
00:42:11,989 --> 00:42:13,908
Have you? Answer me!

604
00:42:16,702 --> 00:42:18,370
Who do you think you are to fire PK?

605
00:42:18,454 --> 00:42:19,955
How dare you mess with him?

606
00:42:20,831 --> 00:42:21,957
Didn't you hear me?

607
00:42:22,458 --> 00:42:24,376
Hey, answer me.

608
00:42:25,794 --> 00:42:27,087
Answer me!

609
00:42:42,102 --> 00:42:43,437
Do you think I'm a joke?

610
00:42:43,938 --> 00:42:45,856
It's not even a big deal,
but you blew it up.

611
00:42:47,233 --> 00:42:49,568
Wait, are you jealous? Are you?

612
00:42:50,361 --> 00:42:54,114
Have I ever said anything
about your infidelity?

613
00:42:55,241 --> 00:42:57,743
At the very least, it shouldn't have
impacted my business.

614
00:42:57,826 --> 00:43:00,079
I didn't do anything.
I didn't even take money from him.

615
00:43:00,162 --> 00:43:02,081
All of you are way disgusting,
so you don't get to do this.

616
00:43:04,041 --> 00:43:06,544
Can you say what you just said
in front of your father?

617
00:43:06,627 --> 00:43:09,338
I'll kill myself
if you dare to do that.

618
00:43:09,964 --> 00:43:11,006
Go ahead.

619
00:43:12,049 --> 00:43:13,259
Go ahead and do that if you can.

620
00:43:16,136 --> 00:43:17,346
This time

621
00:43:18,347 --> 00:43:19,682
you crossed the line for good.

622
00:43:22,309 --> 00:43:23,769
Leave the country immediately.

623
00:43:24,270 --> 00:43:25,771
Don't dream of returning for a while.

624
00:43:27,773 --> 00:43:30,150
Hey!

625
00:43:52,715 --> 00:43:54,675
Why does this always happen
to the Head of Audit?

626
00:43:54,758 --> 00:43:57,011
You're always getting beaten up, hurt

627
00:43:57,678 --> 00:43:58,762
and criticized.

628
00:43:59,805 --> 00:44:00,806
That really hurts.

629
00:44:01,348 --> 00:44:03,142
Be more gentle
and leave your feelings out of it.

630
00:44:06,228 --> 00:44:08,355
Now, stay still.

631
00:44:13,861 --> 00:44:14,945
All done.

632
00:44:18,157 --> 00:44:19,491
Gosh, it hurts.

633
00:44:20,284 --> 00:44:21,493
Don't be a drama queen.

634
00:44:24,079 --> 00:44:25,664
What happened to your legs?

635
00:44:25,748 --> 00:44:27,958
One of them is bruised,
and the other is scraped.

636
00:44:28,042 --> 00:44:31,295
These? I got tackled
by Son Heung-min of Mapo-dong.

637
00:44:31,920 --> 00:44:33,464
Wait, you play soccer?

638
00:44:34,381 --> 00:44:36,508
Gosh, you have so many hobbies.

639
00:44:38,344 --> 00:44:40,012
Did you disinfect your legs?

640
00:44:40,095 --> 00:44:42,431
I'm fine. Leave them.
They'll get better soon.

641
00:44:45,976 --> 00:44:47,269
Stay still.

642
00:44:55,861 --> 00:44:58,280
Models aren't supposed to have
any wounds on their bodies.

643
00:44:59,073 --> 00:45:00,407
Where's your work ethic?

644
00:45:29,937 --> 00:45:32,189
About your question, Mr. Noh...

645
00:45:36,110 --> 00:45:38,237
The real reason
why I keep pushing you away...

646
00:45:45,536 --> 00:45:46,537
I...

647
00:45:54,753 --> 00:45:55,879
I...

648
00:46:01,552 --> 00:46:03,053
It's due next week.

649
00:46:04,179 --> 00:46:05,347
Next week?

650
00:46:08,225 --> 00:46:09,268
Mr. Noh.

651
00:46:09,518 --> 00:46:12,479
The one who just left
was Joo In-a, right?

652
00:46:13,397 --> 00:46:15,357
Gosh, were you getting scolded again?

653
00:46:15,441 --> 00:46:16,734
No, you should get to work.

654
00:46:21,989 --> 00:46:23,115
Ms. Joo.

655
00:46:27,536 --> 00:46:28,871
Let me apologize on her behalf.

656
00:46:28,954 --> 00:46:30,080
It's okay.

657
00:46:41,592 --> 00:46:42,634
Hey.

658
00:46:48,640 --> 00:46:49,683
NON-DISCLOSURE AGREEMENT

659
00:46:49,767 --> 00:46:52,603
It's an NDA that says
you will not say anything

660
00:46:52,686 --> 00:46:54,104
about what you've seen today.

661
00:46:54,188 --> 00:46:57,524
But why? Do you think I'll go out
and tell the whole world

662
00:46:57,608 --> 00:46:59,276
that our vice president's wife
is a crazy psycho?

663
00:46:59,359 --> 00:47:01,028
We're just making sure.

664
00:47:01,195 --> 00:47:03,989
Everyone who was there
had to sign this

665
00:47:04,072 --> 00:47:05,449
so don't overthink it.

666
00:47:05,991 --> 00:47:07,493
You can sign it down there.

667
00:47:12,706 --> 00:47:14,666
You didn't expect that
from the vice president, did you?

668
00:47:16,585 --> 00:47:19,296
He looks perfect and sleek
from the outside.

669
00:47:20,506 --> 00:47:22,424
But once you unravel him

670
00:47:23,634 --> 00:47:24,843
he's one weary man.

671
00:47:28,263 --> 00:47:31,809
Well, I guess everyone
has their share of pain.

672
00:47:33,894 --> 00:47:36,313
Is that why you were drawn to him?

673
00:47:39,483 --> 00:47:41,443
You already knew?

674
00:47:41,527 --> 00:47:44,112
Hey, I can take a hint.

675
00:47:44,947 --> 00:47:46,990
That's why you're in charge of PM.

676
00:47:47,991 --> 00:47:50,285
Joo In-a definitely knows
where to place the right people.

677
00:47:53,539 --> 00:47:56,834
- Are we done here?
- I can also take a hint.

678
00:47:57,793 --> 00:47:59,795
What's going on
between Joo In-a and you?

679
00:48:02,047 --> 00:48:03,257
Is there something special?

680
00:48:08,595 --> 00:48:09,972
Where are you suddenly going?

681
00:48:10,055 --> 00:48:11,682
To find out what our relationship is.

682
00:48:20,858 --> 00:48:22,276
- Hey, Doo-gi.
- Yes?

683
00:48:22,359 --> 00:48:23,694
Where's Ms. Joo?

684
00:48:23,777 --> 00:48:25,612
She took the rest of the day off.
Can you believe it?

685
00:48:25,988 --> 00:48:27,573
She never takes a leave all year long

686
00:48:28,073 --> 00:48:29,324
so something must have happened.

687
00:48:29,992 --> 00:48:32,661
Can you also give me
the rest of the day off?

688
00:48:32,995 --> 00:48:34,079
What?

689
00:48:35,873 --> 00:48:37,624
You're suddenly taking
the rest of the day off?

690
00:48:38,500 --> 00:48:41,962
<i>Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.</i>

691
00:48:42,796 --> 00:48:44,047
Gosh.

692
00:49:10,032 --> 00:49:11,533
JOO IN-A

693
00:49:15,621 --> 00:49:18,749
<i>Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.</i>

694
00:49:24,922 --> 00:49:26,214
MS. JOO...

695
00:49:33,513 --> 00:49:35,265
- Hey, there.
- Hello.

696
00:49:35,515 --> 00:49:36,892
Your face scarred.

697
00:49:47,319 --> 00:49:48,320
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

698
00:49:48,403 --> 00:49:49,571
SHE IS INVOLVED IN AN INAPPROPRIATE
WORKPLACE RELATIONSHIP

699
00:49:54,660 --> 00:49:55,744
<i>Could it be...</i>

700
00:50:44,793 --> 00:50:45,794
Let's see.

701
00:51:05,605 --> 00:51:06,648
Joo In-a.

702
00:51:09,901 --> 00:51:11,069
Ms. Joo!

703
00:51:57,491 --> 00:51:59,034
You came, Ms. Joo.

704
00:51:59,868 --> 00:52:01,870
Don't even get me started, Jae-yeol.

705
00:52:01,953 --> 00:52:04,498
She kept insisting on not coming,
so I had to go to her place

706
00:52:04,581 --> 00:52:06,166
and force her to be here.

707
00:52:06,708 --> 00:52:07,751
Mr. Noh.

708
00:52:11,421 --> 00:52:14,966
I know. You were the guy
who gave the presentation.

709
00:52:15,050 --> 00:52:16,593
What brings you here?

710
00:52:18,011 --> 00:52:19,262
Well, the thing is...

711
00:52:21,973 --> 00:52:24,351
I had something urgent
to share with Ms. Joo.

712
00:52:30,690 --> 00:52:33,443
Goodness. What a passionate employee.

713
00:52:33,527 --> 00:52:36,404
You live up to your reputation.

714
00:52:36,488 --> 00:52:38,323
You can take your time
and talk to him, Ms. Joo.

715
00:52:38,406 --> 00:52:40,033
It's a lunch break anyway.

716
00:52:40,117 --> 00:52:41,701
Yes, he came all the way here

717
00:52:41,785 --> 00:52:43,829
so at least let him have
some fresh raw fish. Stay for lunch.

718
00:52:44,663 --> 00:52:46,164
- Yes, ma'am.
- Let's go.

719
00:53:04,558 --> 00:53:07,144
This must be an event
for the executives.

720
00:53:07,936 --> 00:53:09,437
It's held at a nice place.

721
00:53:10,021 --> 00:53:11,523
What's the urgent matter?

722
00:53:17,154 --> 00:53:18,446
Aren't you going to let me have fish?

723
00:53:19,114 --> 00:53:20,448
It's my favorite.

724
00:53:22,038 --> 00:53:25,124
This is so good.
It's so fresh and has a nice texture.

725
00:53:26,000 --> 00:53:27,877
You should have some, too.

726
00:53:29,879 --> 00:53:33,341
No, I should've made
a lettuce wrap for you.

727
00:53:33,424 --> 00:53:36,761
Now, tell me
what the urgent matter is.

728
00:53:38,221 --> 00:53:39,389
Well, you know.

729
00:53:40,473 --> 00:53:41,516
It's been resolved.

730
00:53:42,850 --> 00:53:43,851
In that while?

731
00:53:44,352 --> 00:53:47,689
You traveled this far for a matter
that could be resolved so quickly?

732
00:53:47,772 --> 00:53:49,691
Isn't it great
that it's been resolved quickly?

733
00:53:52,819 --> 00:53:55,321
Now, open up.

734
00:53:57,907 --> 00:53:59,158
You enjoy your food.

735
00:54:00,326 --> 00:54:01,786
Gosh. You're so cold.

736
00:54:11,713 --> 00:54:13,256
You seem to enjoy it a lot.

737
00:54:14,215 --> 00:54:16,759
Wait, did you really come here
to get raw fish?

738
00:54:16,968 --> 00:54:20,096
It's really good, so here.

739
00:54:20,555 --> 00:54:21,931
You should have some, too.

740
00:54:22,307 --> 00:54:23,766
Don't drink soju on an empty stomach.

741
00:54:24,142 --> 00:54:25,977
Or at least let me drink with you.
Here.

742
00:54:26,936 --> 00:54:28,104
Cheers.

743
00:54:37,864 --> 00:54:39,198
That's nice.

744
00:54:39,532 --> 00:54:41,701
So why did you suddenly take
the rest of the day off?

745
00:54:42,201 --> 00:54:44,203
People were surprised
that you did that.

746
00:54:44,579 --> 00:54:47,290
If I returned to the office
after the executive meeting

747
00:54:48,249 --> 00:54:49,625
people would spread rumors.

748
00:54:53,338 --> 00:54:56,132
If the urgency has been resolved,
let's finish eating and go.

749
00:54:56,215 --> 00:54:59,594
Let's take our time.
Mr. Jeon told us you could do that.

750
00:55:00,720 --> 00:55:01,804
I mean

751
00:55:02,472 --> 00:55:03,765
look at this.

752
00:55:04,098 --> 00:55:06,225
It's so nice to see the sea
for the first time in a while.

753
00:55:09,062 --> 00:55:10,229
It's like we're on a date.

754
00:55:18,154 --> 00:55:20,323
Mr. Noh, you're quite a simple guy.

755
00:55:28,915 --> 00:55:32,126
Yes, so keep it simple and finish
what you were going to say.

756
00:55:32,877 --> 00:55:34,420
- Say what?
- The answer

757
00:55:36,589 --> 00:55:37,840
you were about to give me.

758
00:55:38,341 --> 00:55:40,551
<i>About your question, Mr. Noh...</i>

759
00:55:41,969 --> 00:55:43,930
The real reason
why I keep pushing you away...

760
00:55:47,725 --> 00:55:48,768
I...

761
00:55:53,773 --> 00:55:54,941
Oh, that one.

762
00:56:06,077 --> 00:56:07,203
I...

763
00:56:23,428 --> 00:56:24,429
I forgot.

764
00:56:25,972 --> 00:56:28,641
I completely forgot what it was.
I've been so out of it.

765
00:56:29,684 --> 00:56:31,227
Let me try some raw fish.

766
00:56:34,147 --> 00:56:36,190
This place is delicious.

767
00:56:36,274 --> 00:56:38,109
Enjoy, Mr. Noh.
Do you want some soup too?

768
00:56:38,609 --> 00:56:41,362
Excuse me.
Can we have the spicy fish soup?

769
00:56:41,446 --> 00:56:42,864
And two bowls of rice!

770
00:56:44,866 --> 00:56:45,867
Cheers.

771
00:56:49,287 --> 00:56:50,663
Your glass is empty.

772
00:56:55,168 --> 00:56:56,169
Cheers.

773
00:57:08,514 --> 00:57:10,808
That happened at a coffee shop?

774
00:57:10,975 --> 00:57:12,560
I freaked out.

775
00:57:12,935 --> 00:57:14,770
He came over as if he'd punch me

776
00:57:14,854 --> 00:57:17,940
while everyone was watching
then suddenly knelt.

777
00:57:19,734 --> 00:57:21,903
I can imagine
what your face was like.

778
00:57:23,321 --> 00:57:24,447
Oh, my.

779
00:57:36,375 --> 00:57:37,460
Be careful.

780
00:57:41,172 --> 00:57:43,090
Hey. Don't be so cheeky.

781
00:57:46,594 --> 00:57:49,263
- Hands off.
- You tripped first, girl.

782
00:57:51,265 --> 00:57:52,308
"Girl"?

783
00:57:53,267 --> 00:57:54,894
Do you think you're my equal...

784
00:58:09,825 --> 00:58:11,035
Did you really forget

785
00:58:12,537 --> 00:58:14,080
what you were going to say to me?

786
00:58:17,083 --> 00:58:19,001
Why are you so dishonest?

787
00:58:26,926 --> 00:58:27,927
You.

788
00:58:28,553 --> 00:58:29,554
Why did you come here?

789
00:58:30,096 --> 00:58:31,264
What was the urgent matter?

790
00:58:36,519 --> 00:58:37,812
You lied, too.

791
00:58:39,647 --> 00:58:40,648
Wait, it's...

792
00:58:41,816 --> 00:58:43,317
It's embarrassing.

793
00:58:44,318 --> 00:58:46,821
Actually, I came running after you
because I lost my cool.

794
00:58:47,405 --> 00:58:49,156
I went to your place,
saw you get in Mr. Jeon's car

795
00:58:49,240 --> 00:58:50,992
and took it completely the wrong way.

796
00:58:51,701 --> 00:58:53,786
I lost it and raced all the way here.

797
00:58:54,745 --> 00:58:55,830
Isn't it hilarious?

798
00:58:55,913 --> 00:58:57,331
It's not like I'm your husband.

799
00:58:57,873 --> 00:58:58,958
Wait a second.

800
00:59:00,668 --> 00:59:02,169
Mr. Jeon and I?

801
00:59:07,008 --> 00:59:09,093
Was that why you called my name
in that scary tone?

802
00:59:09,844 --> 00:59:11,554
It sounded like
you wanted to punch him.

803
00:59:11,637 --> 00:59:13,180
Yes, exactly. I've gone crazy.

804
00:59:18,227 --> 00:59:19,895
I've lost a bit of my mind

805
00:59:21,188 --> 00:59:22,231
because of you.

806
00:59:28,487 --> 00:59:29,947
Stop feigning ignorance.

807
00:59:31,532 --> 00:59:32,867
You already know.

808
00:59:36,704 --> 00:59:37,830
You know that I like you.

809
00:59:43,294 --> 00:59:44,503
Hey, look.

810
00:59:46,505 --> 00:59:47,757
Where are you going?

811
00:59:48,549 --> 00:59:49,800
Wait! Come back here!

812
00:59:54,555 --> 00:59:56,182
You said you liked plushies, right?

813
01:00:04,649 --> 01:00:06,776
Now, let's get the plushie.

814
01:00:11,781 --> 01:00:13,366
Grab it. Grab it. Grab it.

815
01:00:28,005 --> 01:00:30,966
You're trying to get that, right?
Because of the gold bar.

816
01:00:31,050 --> 01:00:32,677
You're so materialistic.

817
01:00:33,719 --> 01:00:35,554
Move over. Let me try.

818
01:00:35,930 --> 01:00:38,099
You aren't
supposed to do this recklessly.

819
01:00:38,891 --> 01:00:40,184
You need good skills.

820
01:01:03,416 --> 01:01:04,625
Look.

821
01:01:05,668 --> 01:01:08,087
Right here, you're going to drop...

822
01:01:13,259 --> 01:01:14,301
Down.

823
01:01:16,220 --> 01:01:17,596
You can't win that.

824
01:01:18,305 --> 01:01:19,598
I can tell that this crane machine

825
01:01:19,682 --> 01:01:22,643
holds the claws tightly
only for about three seconds.

826
01:01:23,310 --> 01:01:25,146
And that bear has
metal lumps in its hands

827
01:01:25,229 --> 01:01:26,480
which makes it too heavy to lift.

828
01:01:28,441 --> 01:01:30,401
It doesn't matter
if you try 1,000 or 10,000 times.

829
01:01:30,943 --> 01:01:31,986
You can't win.

830
01:01:33,320 --> 01:01:36,782
It's not that you're unlucky
or not talented enough.

831
01:01:37,992 --> 01:01:40,035
It's just programmed that way.

832
01:01:41,078 --> 01:01:42,288
Something that can't work

833
01:01:43,956 --> 01:01:45,583
can never work even if you're reborn.

834
01:01:53,090 --> 01:01:54,425
That's my answer.

835
01:01:56,177 --> 01:01:57,344
I can't...

836
01:02:01,682 --> 01:02:02,850
be with you.

837
01:02:03,559 --> 01:02:05,102
That's just how I'm set.

838
01:02:07,480 --> 01:02:09,982
First, you're under my authority.

839
01:02:11,150 --> 01:02:13,277
That already is something
I'm not willing to risk.

840
01:02:17,072 --> 01:02:18,240
Also, I believe

841
01:02:19,825 --> 01:02:22,036
you're getting
your feelings confused.

842
01:02:23,037 --> 01:02:25,039
It's probably curiosity or pity.

843
01:02:25,956 --> 01:02:27,124
Think about it.

844
01:02:27,541 --> 01:02:29,877
You've received too much information
about me in a short while.

845
01:02:30,461 --> 01:02:32,963
You've seen me naked,
and you know about my family.

846
01:02:33,798 --> 01:02:35,174
You kept seeing me like this

847
01:02:35,841 --> 01:02:39,678
and began to think,
"She's a poor, lonely woman."

848
01:02:41,180 --> 01:02:42,389
That's probably it.

849
01:02:43,224 --> 01:02:45,309
Don't define how I feel about you.

850
01:02:45,976 --> 01:02:47,520
Well, that was how it began.

851
01:02:49,605 --> 01:02:50,815
Can you deny that?

852
01:02:55,945 --> 01:02:56,946
Is that bad?

853
01:02:57,822 --> 01:02:59,448
Be it pity or curiosity

854
01:02:59,949 --> 01:03:01,575
the feeling of affection
is all the same.

855
01:03:02,493 --> 01:03:04,995
Can you label feelings
into one, pity, and two, love

856
01:03:05,079 --> 01:03:07,790
as if they were elements
on the periodic table?

857
01:03:08,457 --> 01:03:10,292
Wanting to hold the other person,
missing them

858
01:03:10,376 --> 01:03:12,586
feeling bad for them, pitying them

859
01:03:12,670 --> 01:03:15,256
getting curious, and feeling jealous.

860
01:03:18,551 --> 01:03:20,261
Aren't those
all part of liking someone?

861
01:03:28,561 --> 01:03:30,437
I don't like feelings
that stem from pity.

862
01:03:31,647 --> 01:03:33,607
There's nothing more pathetic

863
01:03:35,192 --> 01:03:36,443
and stickier than that.

864
01:03:37,528 --> 01:03:39,905
I can't help you
even if you can't accept that.

865
01:03:41,657 --> 01:03:42,992
Something that can't work

866
01:03:45,202 --> 01:03:46,370
simply can't work.

867
01:04:11,353 --> 01:04:14,523
So you two have never fought?

868
01:04:14,607 --> 01:04:15,774
I'm telling you.

869
01:04:16,191 --> 01:04:18,235
Actually, I've always been cheeky

870
01:04:18,736 --> 01:04:20,487
but he always let me win.

871
01:04:20,571 --> 01:04:21,947
I'm glad to hear that you know.

872
01:04:25,242 --> 01:04:29,496
Doesn't that mean
you adored the managing director?

873
01:04:29,580 --> 01:04:30,998
I still find him adorable.

874
01:04:32,416 --> 01:04:35,544
Oh, my. He must adore you a lot.

875
01:04:36,045 --> 01:04:38,339
Are you reminded of the old days?

876
01:04:38,422 --> 01:04:39,882
Yes, of course, he does.

877
01:04:40,674 --> 01:04:41,759
Are you listening to me?

878
01:04:42,718 --> 01:04:46,722
Does Jae-yeol choose not to talk
or is he unable to talk?

879
01:04:54,396 --> 01:04:55,773
Come on.

880
01:05:06,951 --> 01:05:08,452
Darn it.

881
01:05:23,968 --> 01:05:27,054
<i>Something that can't work
can never work even if you're reborn.</i>

882
01:05:28,013 --> 01:05:29,223
<i>That's my answer.</i>

883
01:05:49,493 --> 01:05:51,245
I apologize
for what happened earlier.

884
01:05:55,541 --> 01:05:57,626
Oh, about your wife slapping me?

885
01:05:58,419 --> 01:06:00,129
All I expect
is a lot of salary in return.

886
01:06:05,384 --> 01:06:06,385
Are you all right?

887
01:06:07,511 --> 01:06:08,804
It's not a big deal.

888
01:06:09,430 --> 01:06:12,266
I can take my blows,
so I'm all right.

889
01:06:20,899 --> 01:06:22,901
I thought you were looking at the sea

890
01:06:24,737 --> 01:06:26,280
but you were
looking into the darkness.

891
01:06:30,325 --> 01:06:32,661
This expensive ocean view hotel
is useless at night.

892
01:06:33,370 --> 01:06:35,998
You can't tell where the sea ends
and where the sky begins.

893
01:06:37,249 --> 01:06:38,459
It's only dark.

894
01:06:39,710 --> 01:06:41,420
But you can still feel it.

895
01:06:43,047 --> 01:06:44,798
The sea breeze blows

896
01:06:45,674 --> 01:06:47,259
and you can hear the waves.

897
01:06:58,896 --> 01:07:01,231
Please excuse me. Get a good rest.

898
01:07:02,024 --> 01:07:03,067
In-a.

899
01:07:11,408 --> 01:07:12,618
Let go.

900
01:07:14,286 --> 01:07:15,370
Let go.

901
01:07:17,331 --> 01:07:18,540
Let go of me.

902
01:07:18,624 --> 01:07:20,584
One moment. In-a, wait.

903
01:07:20,667 --> 01:07:22,377
She wants you to let go.

904
01:07:32,012 --> 01:07:33,013
Let go of her.

905
01:07:42,564 --> 01:07:43,607
See?

906
01:07:45,692 --> 01:07:46,944
Something that can't work

907
01:07:48,195 --> 01:07:49,404
still can work.

908
01:08:11,552 --> 01:08:14,429
FILING FOR LOVE

909
01:08:15,097 --> 01:08:17,641
GUEST APPEARANCE BY OH HYE-WON

910
01:08:42,791 --> 01:08:44,710
{\an8}<i>Actually, we go way back.</i>

911
01:08:44,793 --> 01:08:46,461
{\an8}<i>- It's all in the past.
- I know the vice president</i>

912
01:08:46,545 --> 01:08:48,714
{\an8}<i>has feelings for Ms. Joo In-a.</i>

913
01:08:48,797 --> 01:08:51,508
{\an8}<i>Is this the vice president's
one-sided feeling?</i>

914
01:08:52,134 --> 01:08:54,553
{\an8}<i>Or is there something left
between you two?</i>

915
01:08:54,636 --> 01:08:56,597
{\an8}<i>Do you have anyone like that?</i>

916
01:08:56,680 --> 01:08:58,849
{\an8}<i>Someone who always takes your side
no matter what happens.</i>

917
01:08:58,932 --> 01:09:00,767
{\an8}<i>You have a clinical condition
of acting tough.</i>

918
01:09:00,851 --> 01:09:03,145
{\an8}<i>Who cares if you act a little crazy?</i>

919
01:09:03,478 --> 01:09:05,439
{\an8}<i>I don't care how long it takes.</i>

920
01:09:05,939 --> 01:09:07,733
{\an8}<i>Take a good look at your feelings.</i>

921
01:09:08,734 --> 01:09:10,027
{\an8}I'll wait.

922
01:09:12,905 --> 01:09:14,907
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
